{
  "cutoff_065": 0.65,
  "title": "Acceptance vs delinquency (Fritz BNPL samples)",
  "caption": "Top row: locally scored training_package_1_mse (blue) vs the selected challenger (orange). Bottom row: stored production autogluon_v25 from pre_scored_users (blue) vs the same challenger. Same Fritz 4k users on both rows. Hover a Plotly chart for cutoff and rates. Acceptance = Fritz SQL (TIMESTAMPDIFF ≤ 60). Delinquency = separate 4,000 seasoned CaaS users.",
  "note_html": "\n<p><strong>The curve identity is the same.</strong> At cutoff <em>s</em>:</p>\n<p><code>acceptance = users_approved / (users_below + users_above)</code></p>\n<p>That is the gated yes-share of the whole file: score ≥ <em>s</em> and the three gates\n(<code>name_valid_probability ≥ 0.25</code>, <code>is_confirmed_number = 1</code>,\n<code>geolocation_access = 1</code>), divided by every person in the cohort.\nUnique scores, no <code>round(3)</code>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead><tr><th></th><th>Fritz acceptance</th><th>This dashboard</th></tr></thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr><td>Traffic</td><td>Distinct <code>bnpl.api_requests</code> + TIMESTAMPDIFF ≤ 60</td><td>Same SQL, 4,000-user sample</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Who is kept</td><td><code>autogluon_v25 IS NOT NULL</code></td><td>Same</td></tr>\n<tr><td>Previous score</td><td>Stored <code>autogluon_v25</code></td>\n<td><strong>Top:</strong> local <code>training_package_1_mse</code>. <strong>Bottom:</strong> stored <code>autogluon_v25</code></td></tr>\n<tr><td>New score</td><td>A stored <code>autogluon_v*</code></td><td>Local challenger on both sets</td></tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><strong>Delinquency</strong> is a separate 4,000-user Fritz CaaS draw\n(<code>completed_plans &gt; 0</code>). Past-due / principal, not 1 − pngi_rate.</p>\n",
